course: dictionary
lesson: 5546
title: Words from the past: legionary
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A legionary was a soldier in a legion, a large unit of the ancient Roman army. Read the clues in this sentence: «Legionaries marched about 30 kilometres a day carrying their kit.» Marching all day with heavy kit tells you they were soldiers.
explain: Legionary can also be an adjective, a describing word. It means to do with a legion, so legionary duties would be the jobs done by a legion. Look at the word parts too: legion, then -ary. Your history lessons help as well: roads, forts and walls show what legionaries did.
explain: The example sentence gives more clues. «Built a fortified camp every night» means they built a strong camp each evening, so fortified means strong and protected. «Served for 25 years» means they stayed in the army for a very long time. «At the end they got land or money» tells you they were rewarded when they finished.
fact: A legionary was a soldier in a Roman legion.
fact: A legion was a large unit of the ancient Roman army.
fact: Legionaries built roads, forts and Hadrian's Wall.
fact: Stories show legionaries with a shield, a helmet and a short sword.
fact: Legionaries served for 25 years, and at the end many settled in the provinces, the lands of the empire outside Italy.
exercise: Legionary means what? | A Roman emperor who ruled from Rome | *A soldier in a Roman legion | A kind of stone fort | A traveller who sailed the seas
exercise: «Legionaries built a fortified camp every night.» What does fortified mean here? | Very small | Painted in bright colours | *Strong and protected against attack | Empty and quiet
exercise: In «Legionaries marched about 30 kilometres a day carrying their kit», which word means their equipment and belongings? | marched | *kit | about | kilometres
test: As an adjective, legionary means what? | To do with a school | *To do with a legion | To do with a river | To do with a ship
test: «Legionaries served for 25 years.» How long did a legionary serve? | 52 weeks | *25 years | 2 years | 5 years
exam: Which best describes a legionary? | *A soldier in an ancient Roman legion, with a shield, helmet and short sword | A teacher in a Roman school | A Roman emperor who ruled the empire | A sailor who carried goods to Italy
